# The published-version guard's switch, read by scripts/published-version-guard.sh
# from the committed HEAD — the switch as the commit being judged finds it, so no
# commit can loosen it for itself: warn or block. With warn, an entity changed in
# place at a published version, and a change under a version directory the
# catalog was released with, are reported and pass; with block, both are refused.
# Anything else, or no file at all, blocks.
block
